From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] state file: keep queued songs the database does not know yet

When the state file is restored, each queued song is looked up in the
database and dropped if it is not there.  On EROS Q the database can
lag the SD card at boot: music added while the device was off, a
swapped card, or a database cut short by a cancelled update (see 0005).
The boot update (S96sdscan) runs only after mpd has loaded the state,
so those entries vanish (10-23: 34 of 57), and the next power-off saves
the shorter queue for good.

For the state file loader only (it is the one SongLoader without a
client), fall back to reading the song's tags from the music storage.
A song whose file is really gone is still dropped.  The cost is one
tag read per missing song at startup, and nothing when the db is
current.

---
diff --git a/src/SongLoader.cxx b/src/SongLoader.cxx
index 264d6b0..b4d34b9 100644
--- a/src/SongLoader.cxx
+++ b/src/SongLoader.cxx
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "client/IClient.hxx"
 #include "db/DatabaseSong.hxx"
 #include "storage/StorageInterface.hxx"
+#include "fs/AllocatedPath.hxx"
 #include "song/DetachedSong.hxx"
 #include "PlaylistError.hxx"
 #include "config.h"
@@ -26,8 +27,32 @@ DetachedSong
 SongLoader::LoadFromDatabase(const char *uri) const
 {
 #ifdef ENABLE_DATABASE
-	if (db != nullptr)
-		return DatabaseDetachSong(*db, storage, uri);
+	if (db != nullptr) {
+		try {
+			return DatabaseDetachSong(*db, storage, uri);
+		} catch (...) {
+			/* erosq: only the state file restore has no
+			   client.  The db can lag the card at boot (music
+			   added while off; the boot update runs after mpd
+			   starts), and dropping the queue entries it does
+			   not know yet loses them for good at the next
+			   power-off.  Read the file's tags instead; a song
+			   whose file is gone is still dropped. */
+			if (client != nullptr || storage == nullptr)
+				throw;
+
+			const auto path_fs = storage->MapFS(uri);
+			if (path_fs.IsNull())
+				throw;
+
+			DetachedSong song(uri);
+			if (!song.LoadFile(path_fs))
+				throw;
+
+			song.SetRealURI(storage->MapUTF8(uri));
+			return song;
+		}
+	}
 #else
 	(void)uri;
 #endif
